source='Unverified source leads for independent fact-checking: Smithsonian National Museum of Natural History, https://naturalhistory.si.edu/education/teaching-resources/paleontology ; US Geological Survey, https://www.usgs.gov/programs/national-geologic-map-database . Claim-specific evidence and definitions have not been checked.'
C=[]
def add(i,slug,title,q,answer,wrong,why,recall,recallwhy,labels,svgs):
 C.append(dict(i=i,slug='zoo-deeptime-'+slug,title=title,q=q,answer=answer,wrong=wrong,why=why,recall=recall,recallwhy=recallwhy,labels=labels,svgs=svgs))
add(52,'shell-or-impression','Shell and its imprint','A shell fossil and the hollow it left in surrounding rock are found. Which is the impression?', 'The hollow in the rock',['The retained shell','Both are the original shell'],'The first panel represents a retained shell. The second shows the hollow surface that records its shape: an impression. Both are simplified; preservation can be more complicated.','A pressed leaf is gone but its outline remains in rock. Which is the impression?','The remaining outline is an impression of a leaf.', ['Shell retained','Hollow in rock'], ['<path d="M20 60 Q70 -10 120 60 Z" fill="#d8c6a4" stroke="var(--fg)" strokeWidth="3"/><path d="M45 55 Q70 20 95 55 M60 58 Q70 35 80 58" fill="none" stroke="#805d48" strokeWidth="3"/>','<rect x="14" y="10" width="112" height="58" rx="5" fill="#ccb892"/><path d="M25 58 Q70 -2 115 58" fill="none" stroke="#564637" strokeWidth="5"/>'])
add(54,'burial-exposure','A burial comparison','In this toy comparison, two remains start alike. One stays exposed longer while one is buried sooner. Which is protected from surface scavengers sooner?', 'The earlier-buried remains',['The longer-exposed remains','Neither can be protected'],'In the stipulated comparison the earlier-buried remains are covered sooner, while the other remains stay exposed at the surface. Burial can help preservation, but does not guarantee a fossil.','If two objects are alike and one is covered sooner, which has less time exposed at the surface?','The one covered sooner has less exposure in the stipulated comparison.', ['Exposed longer','Buried sooner'], ['<path d="M8 60 H132" stroke="var(--fg)" strokeWidth="3"/><path d="M38 48 L90 48" stroke="#cfb89a" strokeWidth="10" strokeLinecap="round"/><path d="M70 11 V35 M65 29 L70 36 L75 29" stroke="#d46a58" strokeWidth="3" fill="none"/>','<rect x="8" y="28" width="124" height="36" fill="#a78b6c"/><path d="M8 28 H132" stroke="var(--fg)" strokeWidth="3"/><path d="M38 48 L90 48" stroke="#e8d6b9" strokeWidth="10" strokeLinecap="round"/>'])
add(56,'scavenging-remains','What remains together?','In the pictured toy sequence, a scavenger displaces several bones after death. Which arrangement is harder to interpret as an intact body?', 'The scattered bones',['The connected bones','Both show identical arrangement'],'Before disturbance the toy bones are connected. Afterwards they are scattered. Scattered remains can have many causes: this example illustrates one stipulated process, not proof that a scavenger acted at a real site.','A model skeleton is moved from a connected to a scattered arrangement. Which preserves the original arrangement better?','The connected arrangement retains the original pattern in this model.', ['Connected','Displaced'], ['<circle cx="28" cy="40" r="10" fill="#ddd2ba"/><path d="M40 40 H100 M60 40 L48 65 M75 40 L90 65" stroke="#ddd2ba" strokeWidth="7" strokeLinecap="round"/>','<circle cx="25" cy="22" r="9" fill="#ddd2ba"/><path d="M48 55 L73 46 M92 19 L114 28 M18 60 L35 56" stroke="#ddd2ba" strokeWidth="7" strokeLinecap="round"/>'])
add(57,'hard-part-bias','A fossil sample','In a toy sample, 10 animals have hard parts and 10 have only soft parts. If 6 hard parts and 1 soft part are preserved, which kind dominates the sample?', 'Hard-part remains',['Soft-part remains','They are equally common'],'The panels show 6 hard-part records but only 1 soft-part record from equally sized starting groups. This illustrates preservation bias; the toy numbers are not measured fossil rates.','If 4 shells and 1 soft body survive from equal starting groups, which kind dominates the preserved sample?','Four shells outnumber one soft-body record.', ['Hard: 6 of 10','Soft: 1 of 10'], ['<path d="M12 34 Q22 10 32 34 M44 34 Q54 10 64 34 M76 34 Q86 10 96 34 M12 59 Q22 35 32 59 M44 59 Q54 35 64 59 M76 59 Q86 35 96 59" fill="none" stroke="var(--good)" strokeWidth="4"/><text x="119" y="52" textAnchor="middle" fill="var(--fg)" fontSize="12">6</text>','<path d="M38 48 Q55 19 73 48" fill="none" stroke="var(--good)" strokeWidth="5"/><text x="70" y="69" textAnchor="middle" fill="var(--fg)" fontSize="13">1 record</text>'])
add(59,'layer-not-instant','Two marks in sediment','A modeled sediment layer contains marks formed before and after later material settled on top. Does the whole layer represent one instant?', 'No, it accumulated over time',['Yes, every grain arrived together','The marks must be the same age'],'In the model the lower mark was covered before the upper mark formed. A layer can accumulate over an interval rather than in one instant. Real accumulation rates and interruptions require independent evidence.','If a deposit builds up across a season, must every part have formed on the same day?','No. Material deposited earlier and later can belong to the same deposit.', ['Earlier mark','Later mark'], ['<rect x="8" y="42" width="124" height="25" fill="#c6b18c"/><path d="M42 49 L48 58 L54 49" stroke="#534a3e" strokeWidth="3" fill="none"/>','<rect x="8" y="14" width="124" height="53" fill="#c6b18c"/><path d="M42 48 L48 57 L54 48 M86 21 L92 30 L98 21" stroke="#534a3e" strokeWidth="3" fill="none"/>'])
add(62,'unconformity-gap','Layers at a contact','A sequence is known to have layers A, B and C. At one exposure A and C meet across an erosion surface and B is missing. What can the contact represent?', 'A gap in the local record',['Proof B formed there unchanged','A record of every interval'],'The stipulated sequence includes B, but the exposure shows A directly below C across an erosional surface. That contact can mark missing time locally; the diagram alone does not date the gap.','A known sequence has A, B and C, but a site shows A directly below C at an erosion surface. What might be missing?','The site may omit the interval represented by B.', ['Reference order','Eroded exposure'], ['<rect x="18" y="48" width="104" height="16" fill="#c2aa89"/><rect x="18" y="30" width="104" height="18" fill="#a0b8a5"/><rect x="18" y="12" width="104" height="18" fill="#a4b9c5"/><text x="70" y="24" fill="#202630" textAnchor="middle" fontSize="13">C</text><text x="70" y="43" fill="#202630" textAnchor="middle" fontSize="13">B</text><text x="70" y="61" fill="#202630" textAnchor="middle" fontSize="13">A</text>','<rect x="18" y="41" width="104" height="23" fill="#c2aa89"/><rect x="18" y="12" width="104" height="29" fill="#a4b9c5"/><path d="M18 41 Q38 34 58 41 T98 41 T122 41" fill="none" stroke="#604c38" strokeWidth="3"/><text x="70" y="28" fill="#202630" textAnchor="middle" fontSize="13">C</text><text x="70" y="59" fill="#202630" textAnchor="middle" fontSize="13">A</text>'])
add(63,'index-fossil-match','A clue across sites','Two modeled rock sequences contain the same short-lived, widespread fossil type. What can that shared fossil help scientists do?', 'Correlate the fossil-bearing layers',['Prove the rocks formed at the same place','Measure the fossil’s exact age alone'],'The same marked fossil occurs in one layer at each modeled site. Under the stated short-lived, widespread assumption it helps correlate layers; additional evidence is needed to determine an absolute age.','A short-lived fossil type appears in one layer at each of two distant sites. What can it help match?','It can help correlate the fossil-bearing layers under the stated assumptions.', ['Site A','Site B'], ['<rect x="24" y="12" width="92" height="18" fill="#a4b9c5"/><rect x="24" y="30" width="92" height="18" fill="#c2aa89"/><rect x="24" y="48" width="92" height="18" fill="#a0b8a5"/><circle cx="70" cy="39" r="5" fill="#323642"/>','<rect x="24" y="12" width="92" height="18" fill="#c2aa89"/><rect x="24" y="30" width="92" height="18" fill="#a0b8a5"/><rect x="24" y="48" width="92" height="18" fill="#a4b9c5"/><circle cx="70" cy="21" r="5" fill="#323642"/>'])
add(65,'date-range-not-point','An age measurement','A modeled measurement reports 100 ± 2 million years. Which interval represents that reported uncertainty?', '98 to 102 million years',['100 million years exactly','2 to 100 million years'],'The marked interval runs from 98 to 102 million years for the stated ±2 example. Real radiometric dates require method-specific uncertainty and geological interpretation; this is an arithmetic illustration.','A toy date is 50 ± 3 million years. What range does this represent?','Subtract and add 3 to obtain 47 to 53 million years.', ['Reported center','Stated range'], ['<path d="M12 44 H128" stroke="var(--fg)" strokeWidth="3"/><circle cx="70" cy="44" r="6" fill="var(--good)"/><text x="70" y="68" fill="var(--fg)" textAnchor="middle" fontSize="13">100</text>','<path d="M12 44 H128" stroke="var(--fg)" strokeWidth="3"/><path d="M35 44 H105 M35 35 V53 M105 35 V53" stroke="var(--good)" strokeWidth="5"/><text x="35" y="68" fill="var(--fg)" textAnchor="middle" fontSize="13">98</text><text x="105" y="68" fill="var(--fg)" textAnchor="middle" fontSize="13">102</text>'])
add(69,'pollen-record','Clues from pollen','A sediment sample contains many grains matching a plant group. What can those grains contribute to a reconstruction?', 'Evidence about past vegetation',['Proof of every animal present','The exact date without other evidence'],'The modeled sample contains many grains of one illustrated form. Identified pollen can inform past vegetation, but transport, preservation and identification complicate the interpretation. The toy sample is not field data.','Fossil pollen from several plant groups is found in sediment. What can it help investigate?','Identified pollen can inform a reconstruction of past vegetation.', ['Sample viewed','Grains sorted'], ['<rect x="22" y="12" width="96" height="54" rx="8" fill="#c9b998"/><circle cx="45" cy="30" r="6" fill="#5c6951"/><circle cx="73" cy="40" r="6" fill="#5c6951"/><circle cx="93" cy="25" r="6" fill="#5c6951"/>','<circle cx="30" cy="37" r="8" fill="#7e9d65"/><circle cx="57" cy="37" r="8" fill="#7e9d65"/><circle cx="84" cy="37" r="8" fill="#7e9d65"/><circle cx="111" cy="37" r="8" fill="#7e9d65"/>'])
add(72,'single-vs-assemblage','One clue or many?','One fossil is compared with a group of several fossil types from a stated single layer. Which gives a broader view of the sample?', 'The group of several types',['The one specimen alone','Both contain the same observations'],'The second panel contains several stipulated fossil forms, while the first contains one. An assemblage offers more kinds of evidence, but this does not prove all organisms lived together or that sampling is complete.','Which sample has more distinct observations: one shell type, or three different fossil types?','The three-type sample has more distinct observations.', ['One specimen','Several types'], ['<path d="M35 58 Q70 -1 105 58 Z" fill="#d7c6a5" stroke="var(--fg)" strokeWidth="2"/>','<circle cx="30" cy="38" r="13" fill="#d7c6a5"/><path d="M56 55 Q70 10 84 55 Z" fill="#a8c0b0"/><path d="M100 20 L116 55 M116 20 L100 55" stroke="#c7a883" strokeWidth="5"/>'])
add(80,'mixed-age-assemblage','A mixed collection','A modeled deposit contains one specimen from an older layer and another from a younger layer, both transported into it. Can the mixed deposit alone prove they lived at the same time?', 'No, their source ages differ',['Yes, every fossil must be contemporaneous','The collection fixes one exact age'],'The example combines specimens from two stipulated source ages in one later deposit. Their shared burial place alone does not show that the original animals lived together. Real sites require independent dating and context.','A collection mixes one old and one young specimen. Does being in one box show they lived together?','No. A later collection or deposit can mix specimens from different times.', ['Older source','Younger source'], ['<rect x="6" y="10" width="50" height="50" fill="#b9a381"/><circle cx="31" cy="30" r="10" fill="#e6d9be"/><path d="M58 32 H80 M74 26 L80 32 L74 38" fill="none" stroke="var(--fg)" strokeWidth="3"/><rect x="84" y="14" width="50" height="46" fill="#a2b9ad"/><circle cx="105" cy="38" r="7" fill="#e6d9be"/>','<rect x="6" y="10" width="50" height="50" fill="#9bb8a8"/><path d="M20 40 L30 20 L40 40 Z" fill="#ece2cb"/><path d="M58 32 H80 M74 26 L80 32 L74 38" fill="none" stroke="var(--fg)" strokeWidth="3"/><rect x="84" y="14" width="50" height="46" fill="#a2b9ad"/><circle cx="95" cy="25" r="6" fill="#e6d9be"/><path d="M100 49 L109 32 L118 49 Z" fill="#ece2cb"/>'])
add(81,'habitat-burial','Where did it live?','A toy model shows a bone carried by a stream before burial downstream. Which location does the burial site identify directly?', 'Where the bone was buried',['Exactly where the animal lived','Every place the animal traveled'],'The bone starts upstream in this stipulated scenario and is buried downstream. Its burial site is the direct location of the deposit; the animal’s habitat needs additional evidence. The arrows show a model, not a real find.','If a modeled shell is carried downstream before burial, does the burial point alone fix where its animal lived?','No. Transport can separate the burial location from the living habitat.', ['Upstream','Burial'], ['<path d="M15 48 H124" stroke="var(--good)" strokeWidth="5"/><circle cx="35" cy="34" r="8" fill="#d7c6a5"/><path d="M48 30 H92 M84 23 L93 30 L84 37" fill="none" stroke="var(--fg)" strokeWidth="3"/>','<path d="M15 30 H124" stroke="var(--good)" strokeWidth="5"/><rect x="20" y="30" width="100" height="34" fill="#b9a381"/><circle cx="100" cy="48" r="8" fill="#e0d1b6"/>'])
add(86,'one-vs-many-extinctions','How broad is the loss?','In a toy record, one species disappears in case A; many groups disappear in case B over the stated interval. Which case is the broader loss?', 'Case B',['Case A','Both have the same number of losses'],'The modeled record marks one loss in A and multiple losses across groups in B. This illustrates breadth, not the criteria for naming a real mass extinction: rates, extent and dating require separate evidence.','One toy record loses one species; another loses many groups. Which has the broader loss?','The second record shows loss across more groups in the stated toy example.', ['A: one loss','B: many losses'], ['<circle cx="30" cy="38" r="9" fill="var(--bad)"/><circle cx="60" cy="38" r="9" fill="var(--muted)"/><circle cx="90" cy="38" r="9" fill="var(--muted)"/>','<circle cx="30" cy="38" r="9" fill="var(--bad)"/><circle cx="60" cy="38" r="9" fill="var(--bad)"/><circle cx="90" cy="38" r="9" fill="var(--bad)"/>'])
add(89,'crater-shock-clues','Two kinds of clue','A suspected impact is investigated using a crater-shaped structure and minerals with impact-related shock features. Why inspect both?', 'They are different lines of evidence',['Either alone gives the full history','The minerals make geology unnecessary'],'The modeled investigation separates a large-scale structure from microscopic mineral features. Different observations can support or challenge an impact interpretation; each must be identified and dated independently.','If two independent geological observations are used to investigate an impact, why inspect both?','Different observations can add separate constraints to the interpretation.', ['Structure','Mineral feature'], ['<path d="M12 26 Q70 70 128 26" fill="none" stroke="var(--fg)" strokeWidth="4"/><path d="M12 26 H128" stroke="var(--muted)" strokeWidth="2"/>','<path d="M42 13 L100 20 L94 62 L34 55 Z" fill="#a2b9ca" stroke="var(--fg)" strokeWidth="2"/><path d="M48 20 L80 53 M57 18 L89 51 M67 17 L96 46" stroke="#304b60" strokeWidth="2"/>'])
R={52:['The outline in rock','The vanished leaf itself','Neither can be an impression'],54:['The object covered sooner','The object exposed longer','Both have the same exposure'],56:['The connected arrangement','The scattered arrangement','Both preserve the same arrangement'],57:['Shells','Soft bodies','They are equally frequent'],59:['No; the deposit can build up across multiple days','Yes; all material must arrive in one day','The model supplies no deposition interval'],62:['The interval represented by B','Only the interval represented by A','No time interval can be missing'],63:['The layers containing the fossil','The exact absolute age by itself','The place where both layers formed'],65:['47 to 53 million years','50 million years exactly','3 to 50 million years'],69:['Past vegetation','Every animal present','An exact date without other evidence'],72:['The sample with three types','The sample with one type','Both contain the same number of types'],80:['No; the specimens can have different source ages','Yes; a shared collection proves coexistence','Yes; the deposit determines one exact lifespan'],81:['No; transport can move it before burial','Yes; burial and life locations must match','Yes; a single bone fixes the whole habitat'],86:['The record losing many groups','The record losing one species','Both show equally broad loss'],89:['Different observations can constrain the interpretation','One clue contains the whole history','The mineral feature makes geology unnecessary']}
assert len(C)==14 and len({x['slug'] for x in C})==14
out=Path('src/demos/life')
if any((out/x['slug']).exists() for x in C):raise SystemExit('Refusing to overwrite existing lessons')
template='''"use client";
import { useState } from "react";
import { Lesson } from "@/kit/Lesson";
import { Control, Row } from "@/kit/controls";
const data = __DATA__;
export default function Demo({slug}:{slug:string}) {
 const [step,setStep]=useState(0);
 return <Lesson slug={slug} predict={{question:data.question,options:data.options,answer:data.answer}} exploreHint="Open both evidence panels before comparing them." reveal={()=><p>{data.explanation}</p>}>
 {({locked,interact})=><div>
 <svg viewBox="0 0 320 145" className="stage-svg" role="img" aria-label={step===0 ? "Two evidence panels are hidden." : step===1 ? data.labels[0]+" shown; second panel hidden." : data.labels.join(" and ")+" shown; schematic."}>
 <rect x="5" y="7" width="150" height="125" rx="12" fill="var(--bg-2)" stroke="var(--muted)"/><rect x="165" y="7" width="150" height="125" rx="12" fill="var(--bg-2)" stroke="var(--muted)"/>
 {step>=1 && <g transform="translate(10 14)">__SVG1__</g>}{step>=2 && <g transform="translate(170 14)">__SVG2__</g>}
 <text x="80" y="116" textAnchor="middle" fill="var(--fg)" fontSize="12">{step>=1?data.labels[0]:"Panel 1"}</text><text x="240" y="116" textAnchor="middle" fill="var(--fg)" fontSize="12">{step>=2?data.labels[1]:"Panel 2"}</text>
 </svg><Row><Control style={{minHeight:44}} disabled={locked||step!==0} onClick={()=>setStep(1)}>Open first</Control><Control style={{minHeight:44}} disabled={locked||step!==1} onClick={()=>{setStep(2);interact();}}>Open second</Control></Row>
 <p style={{textAlign:"center",color:"var(--muted)",fontSize:"0.8rem"}}>Illustrative schematic</p></div>}
 </Lesson>;
}
'''
for c in C:
 shift=c['i']%3;raw=[c['answer']]+c['wrong'];options=raw[shift:]+raw[:shift]; data={'question':c['q'],'options':options,'answer':options.index(c['answer']),'explanation':c['why'],'labels':c['labels']}
 demo=template.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)).replace('__SVG1__',c['svgs'][0]).replace('__SVG2__',c['svgs'][1]);p=out/c['slug'];p.mkdir(parents=True);(p/'Demo.tsx').write_text(demo)
 recall={'question':c['recall'],'options':R[c['i']],'answer':0,'why':c['recallwhy']}
 meta={'slug':c['slug'],'title':c['title'],'hook':'Compare two pieces of evidence.','domain':'life','concept':c['slug'],'status':'draft','durationSec':60,'owner':{'categoryManager':'cm-life','builder':'demo-builder'},'learner':{'knows':['Evidence can constrain an interpretation.'],'doesNotKnow':[c['why']]},'misconception':'The first apparent interpretation is the only possible one.','objective':c['q'],'claims':[{'id':f"life.{c['slug']}.c1",'text':c['q']+' '+c['why']+' '+'. '.join(c['labels']),'support':'source','source':source,'status':'unverified'},{'id':f"life.{c['slug']}.c2",'text':'The diagram is an illustrative schematic, not an observation of an actual site.','support':'convention','source':'Diagram convention','status':'unverified'},{'id':f"life.{c['slug']}.c3",'text':c['recall']+' '+c['recallwhy'],'support':'source','source':source,'status':'unverified'}],'confidence':'','recall':recall,'evidence':{'qa':[],'simulatedLearner':[],'pairwise':[],'humanLearners':[]},'version':1}
 (p/'meta.json').write_text(json.dumps(meta,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
notes=Path('company/reviews/zoology-fossil-second');notes.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
(notes/'manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps([{'plan_id':c['i'],'slug':c['slug']} for c in C],indent=2)+'\n')
(notes/'build.md').write_text('''# Fossil/deep-time draft comparisons\n\nFourteen distinct proposed questions are implemented as illustrative schematic comparisons. These are not observed sites, measured preservation rates, fourteen independently validated simulations, or science-reviewed lessons. The common interaction opens two retained panels after prediction. Every claim and the broad source leads are unverified. Specific source matching, overlap audit, science, accessibility, visual pedagogy, browser/phone fit and learner review remain open.\n\nThe preservation bias, sediment, uncertainty and extinction examples are explicitly stipulated toy models. The index-fossil lesson assumes a short-lived, widespread taxon. The transport example stipulates movement rather than inferring it from a burial location. Fossil impressions, taphonomy and impact evidence require source-specific scientific review.\n\n## Pre-flight v1\n\nEach locked stage has two hidden panels; titles and hooks do not state the answer. Both buttons are 44 px minimum and open one panel each; the second enables the reveal. Both evidence panels remain visible at reveal. The parent must check DOM-order controls, Reset/reload behavior and a 390×844 screenshot in a real browser; these have not been tested. The scenes contain short labels, and the explanatory text names only revealed evidence or stipulated scenario conditions. Source-text and visual accuracy remain unverified.\n''')
print('generated',len(C))
